      "widgets_values": [
        "## Breeze TTS 2\n\n[Breeze TTS 2](https://huggingface.co/BreezeBlue/Breeze-TTS-2) is BreezeBlue's open-weight real-time TTS model: it ranks #1 among open-weight models on the Artificial Analysis TTS leaderboard and speaks natural **English and Chinese** from a single checkpoint.\n\n## ComfyUI links\n- [saganaki22/ComfyUI-Breeze-TTS-2](https://github.com/saganaki22/ComfyUI-Breeze-TTS-2)\n- [drbaph/Breeze-TTS-2-comfyui](https://huggingface.co/drbaph/Breeze-TTS-2-comfyui) (bf16 + int8 builds; the loader auto-downloads)\n\n## About this workflow\n\nVoice cloning: **Load Model** -> **Whisper Transcribe** (builds the reference transcript) -> **Voice Clone**.\n\n**Key inputs**\n\n- **model**: `int8-hybrid` (default - bf16 speed at ~5.5 GiB peak VRAM), `bf16` (fastest, ~7.5 GiB), `int8-convrot` (smallest, ~5.2 GiB, slower decode), `int8-text-encoder` (decode path bf16)\n- **dtype / attention**: auto picks bf16 + flash_attention (falls back to sdpa); sageattention is supported\n- **reference_audio / reference_text**: a clean clip and its exact transcript (the Whisper node transcribes for you)\n- **text**: vocal events work inline - `(laugh)`, `(sigh)`, `(cough)`, `(clears throat)` in English, `[笑]`, `[叹气]` in Chinese\n- **cfg_scale**: 1.0 clones the reference as-is; the Design/Direction nodes default to 4 for instruction-following\n- **seed**: repeatable when positive, 0 keeps the current random state\n\nTry the **Voice Design** node for reference-free synthesis and **Voice Direction** to steer a cloned voice with an instruction. Output is 24 kHz mono.\n\n[Saganaki22/ComfyUI-Breeze-TTS-2](https://github.com/Saganaki22/ComfyUI-Breeze-TTS-2)"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
